##### docker compose ####
docker yaml file to create container
create one directroies
-> mkdir docker-compose
cd docker-compose
-> make one file with same name 
docker-compose.yml


version:  "3.8"
services:
  webapp:
    image:  nginx
    ports: 
      - "8000:80" 
     
-> docker compose up -d 
  to create container

-> docker compose down 
 for delete container

docker yaml file for multiple container

version:  "3.8"
services:
  webapp:
    image:  nginx
    ports: 
      - "8000:80"

  webapp1:
    image:  nginx
    ports: 
      - "8001:80"
 with this configuration u can create two container

if u wants to create a yml file with another name
so u can 
but with this change you run up command like this 
  -> docker compose -f <your_file_name> up -d
or to down container
 -> docker compose -f <your_file_name> down


